SMPS VS UPS 
===========================

1. SMPS
   - Converts AC power into stable DC power for electronic devices.

   UPS
   - Provides backup power when the main electricity supply fails.

2. SMPS
   - Does not normally provide power after an electricity outage.

   UPS
   - Uses a battery to keep devices running during an electricity outage.



SMPS - AT COLLEGE
--------------

1. Desktop Computer
   - Provides efficient and stable DC power to computer components.

2. Computer Monitor
   - Converts AC power into the required DC voltage for the monitor.

3. Projector
   - Supplies stable power to operate the projector's electronic circuits.


UPS - AT OFFICE
---------------------

1. Wi-Fi Router 
   - Keeps the router running during short power cuts.

2. Office Computer 
   - Provides backup power during power cuts and prevents sudden shutdowns.




